{"abstract":"In real-world machine learning (ML) pipelines, datasets are continuously growing. Models must incorporate this new training data to improve generalization and adapt to potential distribution shifts. The cost of model retraining is proportional to how frequently the model is retrained and how much data it is trained on, which makes the naive approach of retraining from scratch each time impractical. We present Modyn, a data-centric end-to-end machine learning platform. Modyn's ML pipeline abstraction enables users to declaratively describe policies for continuously training a model on a growing dataset. Modyn pipelines allow users to apply data selection policies (to reduce the number of data points) and triggering policies (to reduce the number of trainings). Modyn executes and orchestrates these continuous ML training pipelines. The system is open-source and comes with an ecosystem of benchmark datasets, models, and tooling. We formally discuss how to measure the performance of ML pipelines by introducing the concept of composite models, enabling fair comparison of pipelines with different data selection and triggering policies. We empirically analyze how various data selection and triggering policies impact model accuracy, and also show that Modyn enables high throughput training with sample-level data selection.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Böther, Maximilian","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Gsteiger, Viktor","Holzinger, Robin","Ma, Xianzhe","Tözün, Pinar","Klimovic, Ana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798527"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Data centric AI","Machine Learning Pipelines","Online learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modyn data centric machine learning pipeline orchestration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3709705","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Ties Robroek is supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark’s Sapere Aude program (grant agreement number 0171-00061B)."],"id":"S01-000.00-798527","ids":["itu-3c4867ca-0f54-4916-93c9-ee174f2843d9"],"keyword":["data-centric ai","machine learning pipelines","online learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-19092CC39DB1CB3CDBA0E1B8E3F5D95C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3709705","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mboether.com/assets/pdf/bother2025modyn.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maximilian","key":"bötherpau","last":"Böther","name":"Böther, Maximilian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktor","key":"gsteigerpau","last":"Gsteiger","name":"Gsteiger, Viktor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"holzingerpau","last":"Holzinger","name":"Holzinger, Robin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianzhe","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Xianzhe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pınar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","name_org":"Tözün, Pınar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana","key":"klimovicpau","last":"Klimovic","name":"Klimovic, Ana","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-3c4867ca-0f54-4916-93c9-ee174f2843d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modyn: Data-Centric Machine Learning Pipeline Orchestration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798527","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The process of training and serving deep learning (DL) models is computationally expensive, mandating the use of powerful and expensive accelerators such as GPUs and TPUs. Furthermore, the prevalence of GPUs in data centers today motivate developing database systems that can leverage the available GPU resources. Both the latency of DL tasks and database queries and high utilization of these accelerators depend on how efficiently we can move the data to the accelerators. Given today’s dataset sizes, fitting everything in GPU or even CPU memory is not always feasible or can be expensive. The I/O path while fetching the data from disks, however, still dominantly relies on CPUs. In this work, we take a step toward understanding today’s landscape for optimizing the I/O path for reading data to GPUs from disks, with a focus on SSDs. First, we review the prominent technologies that target GPU-centric storage accesses. Then, we dive deeper into BaM, as the state-of-the-art method for GPU-centric storage, and evaluate its performance in comparison to the state-of-theart CPU-centric storage interface SPDK. Our results demonstrate that while BaM is able to match the performance of SPDK without involving CPUs on the I/O path, this comes at the cost of a very high GPU use. Finally, we highlight future research directions to enable an I/O path that is both efficient and easy-to-adopt for data-intensive systems that use GPUs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Torp, Karl B.","Lund, Simon A. F.","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828164"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Samsung"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"path to gpu initiated i o for data intensive systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3736227.3736232","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828164","ids":["itu-87959894-b706-4946-a939-7e9f55e8f638"],"keyword":["Data-Intensive Systems","GPU-Centric IO","GPU-Initiated IO","SSDs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FCB425A43853A91E2F351F4BF2909D4F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3736227.3736232","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Miscellaneous","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Samsung"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl B.","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","name":"Torp, Karl B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon A. F.","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Simon A. F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3736227.3736232","isbn":["9798400719400"],"pages":"1-9","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 21st International Workshop on Data Management on New Hardware, DaMoN 2025, Berlin, Germany, June 22-27, 2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013054039"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-87959894-b706-4946-a939-7e9f55e8f638"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Path to GPU-Initiated I/O for Data-Intensive Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828164","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Machine learning (ML) enables forecasts, even in real-time, at ever lower cost and better accuracy. Today, data scientists are able to collect more data, access that data faster, and apply more complex data analysis than ever. As a result, ML impacts a variety of fields such as healthcare, finance, and entertainment. The advances in ML are mainly thanks to the exponential evolution of hardware, the availability of the large datasets, and the emergence of machine learning frameworks, which hide the complexities of the underlying hardware, boosting the productivity of data scientists. On the other hand, the computational need of the powerful ML models has increased several orders of magnitude in the past decade. A state-of-the-art large language processing model can cost of millions dollars to train in the cloud [The AI Index Report, 2024] without accounting for the electricity cost and carbon footprint [Dodge et al, 2022][Wu et al, 2024]. This makes the current rate of increase in model parameters, datasets, and compute budget unsustainable. To achieve a more sustainable progress in ML in the future, it is essential to invest in more resource-/energy-/cost-efficient solutions. In this Dagstuhl Seminar, our main goal was to reason critically about how we build software and hardware for end-to-end machine learning. The crowd was composed of experts from academia and industry across fields of data management, machine learning, compilers, systems, and computer architecture covering expertise of algorithmic optimizations in machine learning, job scheduling and resource management in distributed computing, parallel computing, and data management and processing. During the seminar, we explored how to improve ML resource efficiency through a holistic view of the ML landscape, which includes data preparation and loading, continual retraining of models in dynamic data environments, compiling ML on specialized hardware accelerators, hardware/software co-design for ML, and serving models for real-time applications with low-latency requirements and constrained resource environments. We hope that the discussions and the work planned during the seminar will lead to increased awareness for understanding the utilization of modern hardware and kickstart future developments to minimize hardware underutilization while still enabling emerging applications powered by ML.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Balmau, Oana","Boehm, Matthias","Klimovic, Ana","Pietzuch, Peter R.","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798550"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","McGill University","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","Technical University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Data management","Energy efficiency","Machine learning","Resource efficiency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resource efficient machine learning dagstuhl seminar 000000024311","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/DAGREP.14.7.153","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798550","ids":["itu-a6b082c0-83fb-4f3d-940b-c880f0187595"],"keyword":["Data Management","Energy-Efficiency","Hardware-Software Co-Design","Machine learning","Modern Hardware","Resource-efficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8B49AC3398166E3243B27EEA6D8BC487"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/DAGREP.14.7.153","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/04dagstuhl-reports/volume14/issue07/24311/DagRep.14.7.153/DagRep.14.7.153.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Imperial College London","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oana","key":"balmaupau","last":"Balmau","name":"Balmau, Oana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"boehmpau","last":"Boehm","name":"Boehm, Matthias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana","key":"klimovicpau","last":"Klimovic","name":"Klimovic, Ana","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter R.","key":"pietzuchpau","last":"Pietzuch","name":"Pietzuch, Peter R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/dagrep.14.7.153","issn":["21925283"],"issue":"7","journal":"Dagstuhl Reports","pages":"153-169","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Dagstuhl Reports","volume":"14"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a6b082c0-83fb-4f3d-940b-c880f0187595"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resource-Efficient Machine Learning (Dagstuhl Seminar 24311)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798550","year":"2025","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"For almost 40 years, Gray and Putzolu’s five-minute rule has helped quickly guide system architects to the break-even point between memory caching and direct local storage access. We believe similar rules of thumb are needed for object caches and storage in disaggregated cloud database system designs. However, it is not straightforward to adapt the established rules to the cloud as they presume fixed hardware, while, in the cloud, resources are dynamic and costs are determined by usage. This paper reviews requirements driving object caches, analyzes the design space, defines a cost model, and proposes new rules of thumb to help system designers determine when caches become cost-effective for analytical workloads in the cloud. While perhaps unsurprising, our analysis on AWS shows that caches are beneficial when a system makes (1) two requests per hour for latency-sensitive workloads, or (2) seven requests per second for non-latency-sensitive workloads. These results are consistent with and help explain the near ubiquity of object store caches in cloud analytics systems.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Duwe, Kira","Anadiotis, Angelos","Lamb, Andrew","Lersch, Lucas","Leskes, Boaz","Ritter, Daniel","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798569"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amazon Web Services AI Labs","InfluxData","Laboratory of Cognitive Neuroscience, EPFL","MotherDuck","Oracle Corporation","SAP Research"],"keyword":["Caching","Cloud"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the five minute rule for the cloud caching in analytics systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.vldb.org/cidrdb/papers/2025/p4-duwe.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798569","ids":["itu-ef94986d-6572-4fe0-8a9e-dbc302080cf5"],"keyword":["Caching","Cloud","five-minute rule"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ACF0B0CC7DE2E9C8189BF94618CC06F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.vldb.org/cidrdb/papers/2025/p4-duwe.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"laboratory of cognitive neuroscience epfl","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Laboratory of Cognitive Neuroscience, EPFL","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"oracle corporation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Oracle Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"influxdata","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"InfluxData","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"amazon web services ai labs","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Amazon Web Services AI Labs","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"motherduck","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"MotherDuck","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"sap research","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"SAP Research","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kira","key":"duwepau","last":"Duwe","name":"Duwe, Kira","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Angelos","key":"anadiotispau","last":"Anadiotis","name":"Anadiotis, Angelos","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"lambpau","last":"Lamb","name":"Lamb, Andrew","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucas","key":"lerschpau","last":"Lersch","name":"Lersch, Lucas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Boaz","key":"leskespau","last":"Leskes","name":"Leskes, Boaz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Daniel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Pınar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","name_org":"Tözün, Pınar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Conference on Innovative Data Systems Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ef94986d-6572-4fe0-8a9e-dbc302080cf5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Five-Minute Rule for the Cloud: Caching in Analytics Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798569","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Machine learning (ML) benchmarks are crucial for evaluating the performance, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems, especially as the adoption of complex ML pipelines, such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), continues to grow. These pipelines introduce intricate execution graphs that require more advanced benchmarking approaches. Additionally, collocating workloads can improve resource efficiency but may introduce contention challenges that must be carefully managed. Detailed insights into resource utilization are necessary for effective collocation and optimized edge deployments. However, existing benchmarking frameworks often fail to capture these critical aspects.We introduce a modular end-to-end ML benchmarking framework designed to address these gaps. Our framework emphasizes modularity and reusability by enabling reusable pipeline stages, facilitating flexible benchmarking across diverse ML workflows. It supports complex workloads and measures their end-to-end performance. The workloads can be collocated, with the framework providing insights into resource utilization and contention between the concurrent workloads.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bayer, Robert","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818243"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep learning","Edge computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a modular end to end machine learning benchmarking framework","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818243","identifier":[{"id":"105003119925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep Learning","Edge Computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A776E7A4C0A5304F8C95A70568919C38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://robertbayer.github.io/publication/towards-modular-benchmark/towards-modular-benchmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","locid":"71115e9d-836f-409e-8c75-27d2de3e9caa","name":"Bayer, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards A Modular End-To-End Machine Learning Benchmarking Framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818243","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Deep learning training is an expensive process that extensively uses GPUs. However, not all model training saturates modern powerful GPUs. To create guidelines for such cases, this paper examines the performance of the different collocation methods available on NVIDIA GPUs: naïvely submitting multiple processes on the same GPU using multiple streams, utilizing Multi-Process Service (MPS), and enabling the MultiInstance GPU (MIG). Our results demonstrate that collocating multiple model training runs yields significant benefits, leading to up to three times training throughput despite increased epoch time. On the other hand, the aggregate memory footprint and compute needs of the models trained in parallel must fit the available memory and compute resources of the GPU. MIG can be beneficial thanks to its interference-free partitioning but can suffer from sub-optimal GPU utilization with dynamic or mixed workloads. In general, we recommend MPS as the best-performing and most flexible form of collocation for a single user submitting training jobs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747244"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collocation methods","Compute resources","Deep learning training","GPU utilization","Memory footprint","Model training","Multi Instance GPU MIG","Multi Process Service MPS","NVIDIA GPUs","Training throughput"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an analysis of collocation on gpus for deep learning training","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/collocation_analysisi_euromlsys2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747244","identifier":[{"id":"85192265987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8b5e5d8e-ab9e-4d7b-90f5-806f4ae31520"],"keyword":["Collocation methods","Compute resources","Deep learning training","GPU utilization","Memory footprint","Model training","Multi-Instance GPU (MIG)","Multi-Process Service (MPS)","NVIDIA GPUs","Training throughput"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1622DC3C16BF5AE7FC02BA344E120AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/collocation_analysisi_euromlsys2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ehsan","key":"yousefzadehaslmiandoabpau","last":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab","locid":"ac400e55-5188-4efd-872a-12df089e7068","name":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","orcid":"0000-0003-0156-1435","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3642970.3655827","isbn":["9798400705410"],"pages":"81-90","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 4th Workshop on Machine Learning and Systems, EuroMLSys 2024, Athens, Greece, 22 April 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192265987"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8b5e5d8e-ab9e-4d7b-90f5-806f4ae31520"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Analysis of Collocation on GPUs for Deep Learning Training","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747244","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Satellites have become more widely available due to the reduction in size and cost of their components. As a result, there has been an advent of smaller organizations having the ability to deploy satellites with a variety of data-intensive applications to run on them. One popular application is image analysis to detect, for example, land, ice, clouds, etc. for Earth observation. However, the resource-constrained nature of the devices deployed in satellites creates additional challenges for this resource-intensive application. In this paper, we present our work and lessons-learned on building an Image Processing Unit (IPU) for this satellite. We first highlight the resource constraints based on a deployed satellite performing machine learning on satellite imagery in orbit, including the required latency, power budget, and the network bandwidth limitations driving the need for such a solution. We then investigate the performance of a variety of edge devices (comparing CPU, GPU, TPU, and VPU) for deep-learning-based image processing on satellites. Our goal is to identify devices that are flexible when the workload changes while satisfying the power and latency constraints of satellites. Our results demonstrate that hardware accelerators such as ASICs and GPUs are essential for meeting the latency requirements. However, state-of-the-art edge devices with GPUs may draw too much power for deployment on a satellite.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bayer, Robert","Priest, Julian","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747252"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Earth observation","Edge computing","Image data analysis","Internet of Things","Machine learning","Satellites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reaching the edge of the edge image analysis in space","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/Image-analysis-in-space-deem.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747252","identifier":[{"id":"85196669433","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9d387955-d99f-47de-bff1-b3a3bf62ddd2"],"keyword":["Edge Computing","Machine learning","earth observation","image data analysis","internet of things","satellites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69F20BAC9F0AF937B1528A5916B38209"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/Image-analysis-in-space-deem.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","locid":"71115e9d-836f-409e-8c75-27d2de3e9caa","name":"Bayer, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"priestpau","last":"Priest","name":"Priest, Julian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3650203.3663330","pages":"29-38","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Eighth Workshop on Data Management for End-to-End Machine Learning, DEEM 2024, Santiago, AA, Chile, 9 June 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196669433"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9d387955-d99f-47de-bff1-b3a3bf62ddd2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reaching the Edge of the Edge: Image Analysis in Space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747252","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Internet of Things (IoT) and edge devices have grown in their application fields due to machine learning (ML) models and their capacity to classify images into previously known labels, working close to the end-user. However, the model might be trained with several convolutional neural network (CNN) architectures that can affect its performance when developed in hardware-constrained environments, such as edge devices. In addition, new training trends suggest using transfer learning techniques to get an excellent feature extractor obtained from one domain and use it in a new domain, which has not enough images to train the whole model. In light of these trends, this work benchmarks the most representative CNN architectures on emerging edge devices, some of which have hardware accelerators. The ML models were trained and optimized using a small set of images obtained in IoT environments and using transfer learning. Our results show that unfreezing until the last 20 layers of the model’s architecture can be fine-tuned correctly to the new set of IoT images depending on the CNN architecture. Additionally, quantization is a suitable optimization technique to shrink 2× or 3× times the model leading to a lighter memory footprint, lower execution time, and battery consumption. Finally, the Coral Dev Board can boost 100× the inference process, and the EfficientNet model architecture keeps the same classification accuracy even when the model is adopted to a hardware-constrained environment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rosero-Montalvo, Paul D.","Tözün, Pinar","Hernandez, Wilmar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747254"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmark testing","Computational modeling","Convolutional Neural Networks CNNs","Data models","Quantization signal","Training","Transfer learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized cnn architectures benchmarking in hardware constrained edge devices in iot environments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/JIOT.2024.3369607","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747254","identifier":[{"id":"85186097388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9f4c0db0-28df-4ae1-99ff-da701171f82a"],"keyword":["Benchmark testing","Computational Modeling","Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)","Data models","Quantization (signal)","Training","Transfer Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DC64E01D2FCBA3F7CFE2450E11325718"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/JIOT.2024.3369607","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul D.","key":"roseromontalvopau","last":"Rosero-Montalvo","name":"Rosero-Montalvo, Paul D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wilmar","key":"hernandezpau","last":"Hernandez","name":"Hernandez, Wilmar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/jiot.2024.3369607","issn":["23274662"],"issue":"11","journal":"IEEE Internet of Things Journal","pages":"20357-20366","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Internet of Things Journal","title_org":"IEEE Internet Things Journal","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186097388"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9f4c0db0-28df-4ae1-99ff-da701171f82a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Optimized CNN Architectures Benchmarking in Hardware-Constrained Edge Devices in IoT Environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747254","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Standardized benchmarks are crucial to ensure a fair comparison of performance across systems. While extremely valuable, these benchmarks all use a setup where the workload is well-defined and known in advance. Unfortunately, this has led to overly-tuning data management systems for particular benchmark workloads such as TPC-H or TPC-C. As a result, benchmarking results frequently do not reflect the behavior of these systems in many real-world settings since workloads often significantly vary from the “known” benchmarking workloads. To address this issue, we present surprise benchmarking , a complementary approach to the current standardized benchmarking where “unknown” queries are exercised during the evaluation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Benson, Lawrence","Binnig, Carsten","Bodensohn, Jan-Micha","Lorenzi, Federico","Luo, Jigao","Porobic, Danica","Rabl, Tilmann","Sanghi, Anupam","Sears, Russell","Tözün, Pinar","Ziegler, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747264"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CrystalDB","Darmstadt University of Technology","Hasso Plattner Institute","Oracle Corporation","Technical University of Munich","TigerBeetle"],"keyword":["Benchmarking","Database"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surprise benchmarking the why what and how","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/Surprise_Benchmarking_Vision_Paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747264","identifier":[{"id":"85197238834","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c8197d9c-10ee-437a-8829-c39b3eee125e"],"keyword":["Benchmarking","Database"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-79AFE2327E7C1C09D0F45EDCFAB80C62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/Surprise_Benchmarking_Vision_Paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"darmstadt university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Darmstadt University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"tigerbeetle","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"TigerBeetle","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"oracle corporation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Oracle Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"hasso plattner institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasso Plattner Institute","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"crystaldb","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"CrystalDB","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lawrence","key":"bensonpau","last":"Benson","name":"Benson, Lawrence","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"binnigpau","last":"Binnig","name":"Binnig, Carsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan-Micha","key":"bodensohnpau","last":"Bodensohn","name":"Bodensohn, Jan-Micha","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Federico","key":"lorenzipau","last":"Lorenzi","name":"Lorenzi, Federico","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jigao","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Jigao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Danica","key":"porobicpau","last":"Porobic","name":"Porobic, Danica","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Tilmann","key":"rablpau","last":"Rabl","name":"Rabl, Tilmann","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anupam","key":"sanghipau","last":"Sanghi","name":"Sanghi, Anupam","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Russell","key":"searspau","last":"Sears","name":"Sears, Russell","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"zieglerpau","last":"Ziegler","name":"Ziegler, Tobias","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3662165.3662763","isbn":["9798400706691"],"pages":"1-8","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Tenth International Workshop on Testing Database Systems, DBTest 2024, Santiago, Chile, 9 June 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197238834"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c8197d9c-10ee-437a-8829-c39b3eee125e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Surprise Benchmarking: The Why, What, and How","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747264","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DEI) initiative started as the Diversity/Inclusion initiative in 2020 [4]. The current report summarizes our activities in 2022. Our responsibility as a community is to ensure that attendees of DB conferences feel included, irrespective of their scientific perspective and personal background. One of the first steps was to establish the role of the DEI chairs at DB Conferences, with the DEI team dedicated to providing leadership to help our community achieve this goal. In this leadership role, the DEI team is advising DEI chairs at DB conferences, serving as a memory of DEI events at conferences, building an agreed-upon vision, and committing to working together to devise a set of measures for achieving DEI. That is pursued via actions led by our core members (Figure 1) and liaisons of individual executive bodies (Figure 2): REACH OUT collects data and experiences from our community. INCLUDE monitors and recommends inclusion efforts. ORGANIZE focuses on in-conference organization efforts, such as adopting a code of conduct. INFORM communicates through various channels. SUPPORT coordinates DEI support from executive bodies and sponsors. SCOUT collates DEI efforts from other communities. COORDINATE manages all actions. Two new actions: MEDIA preserves and disseminates the digital media produced by DEI@DB events. ETHICS establishes and promotes ethics guidelines for publications in our community.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Amer-Yahia, Sihem","Agrawal, Divyakant","Amsterdamer, Yael","Bhowmick, Sourav S.","Bonifati, Angela","Borovica-Gajic, Renata","Camacho-Rodríguez, Jesús","Catania, Barbara","Chrysanthis, Panos K.","Curino, Carlo","Darmont, Jérôme","Dobbie, Gillian","Abbadi, Amr El","Floratou, Avrilia","Freire, Juliana","Jindal, Alekh","Kalogeraki, Vana","Maiyya, Sujaya","Meliou, Alexandra","Mohanty, Madhulika","Omidvar-Tehrani, Behrooz","Özcan, Fatma","Peterfreund, Liat","Rahayu, Wenny","Sadiq, Shazia","Sellami, Sana","Sirin, Utku","Tan, Wang-Chiew","Thuraisingham, Bhavani","Tian, Yuanyuan","Tözün, Pinar","Vargas-Solar, Genoveva","Yadwadkar, Neeraja J.","Zakhary, Victor","Zhang, Meihui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718868"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","China","France","Greece","Israel","Italy","New Zealand","Singapore","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["Aix-Marseille University","All Global Affiliations","Athens University of Economics and Business","Bar-Ilan University","Beijing Institute of Technology","CERSA/CNRS France","Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne","Google Inc.","Hebrew University of Jerusalem","IBM Research – Almaden","La Trobe University","Laboratoire d'informatique de Grenoble","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","Microsoft Research","Nanyang Technological University","New York University","Oracle Corporation","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","The Ohio State University","The University of Auckland","The University of Queensland","University of California","University of Genoa","University of Massachusetts","University of Melbourne","University of Pittsburgh","University of Texas","University of Waterloo","Université de Lyon, CNRS"],"keyword":["Community engagement","Conference Management","Diversity","Equity","Inclusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diversity equity and inclusion activities in database conferences a 000000002022 report","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://sigmodrecord.org/authors/","type":"loc","url":"htt